    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "olnF9",
      "x": 3080,
      "y": 920,
      "name": "Rationale C",
      "width": 1400,
      "height": 150,
      "content": "CONCEPT C — FEED + ROSTER   ·   drift as a FIRST-CLASS object (answers §9.4 & §9.2).\nTop: a DRIFT FEED of full cards — CLAIMED vs VERIFIED as two labelled, differently-styled blocks (documentary sans vs instrument mono), delta as the headline. Bottom: an ambient ROLE-COVERAGE MATRIX — 7 role columns aligned so the gaps (which drive itqan installs) are scannable at a glance.\n+ Optimises: separates ‘act now’ (cards) from ‘ambient state’ (matrix); roomy claim/fact; role gaps read as a grid.\n− Sacrifices: a project appears twice (feed + roster); the feed grows with drift count, so it scales worst under many simultaneous drifts."
    },
