    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "XuPdZ",
      "x": 1540,
      "y": 920,
      "name": "Rationale B",
      "width": 1400,
      "height": 150,
      "content": "CONCEPT B — TRIAGE   ·   claim-vs-fact as EDITORIAL correction.  ◀ recommended\nOne dense fixed-height scan-line per project, sorted by severity, with a left severity rail for peripheral/ambient glance. Drift rows expand a second tier: the claim STRUCK THROUGH → the mono correction → a stale badge (copy-editing treatment). Two-tier row solves heterogeneity: scan-line fixed for all; detail only where there is drift; sync rows stay one line.\n+ Optimises: fastest 3-second read + ambient rail; compact; scan-line never breaks.\n− Sacrifices: the drift sentence is squeezed onto one line (truncation risk); fixed columns can crowd long branches."
    },
